<title>CHINA: Shanghai Metal Exchange to close for Labour Day.</title>
<headline>Shanghai Metal Exchange to close for Labour Day.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Shanghai Metal Exchange will close on Thursday and Friday for the Labour Day holiday, the exchange said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Trading will resume next Monday, it said.</p>
<p>The most actively traded August 1997 copper contract ended Wednesday at an intraday low of 23,600 yuan ($2,845) per tonne, losing 50 yuan. It opened at 23,650 and hit a high of 23,700 yuan per tonne.</p>
<p>($1=8.2948 yuan)</p>
</text>
